cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference LORM in a paper, standard, or internal policy document,
  please cite the specification version you worked from — the model is
  normative, so which version you read matters.
title: "LORM — Layered Operational Responsibility Model"
abstract: >-
  A specification grading the operational autonomy of systems that participate
  in operational decisions on a single axis: who authorized the action — nobody
  needed (observing, explaining), a human per action, or an explicit, versioned,
  expiring policy. Six levels (L0-L5) are assigned per capability rather than
  per system, earned by measured outcomes and demoted automatically on
  incidents, rollbacks, verification failures, telemetry loss, or policy expiry.
  The repository also contains a reference implementation as a Claude Code
  plugin: an agent skill, policy-driven enforcement hooks, and a machine-
  readable policy schema.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Argyronix"
    website: "https://argyronix.com"
    email: "contact@argyronix.com"
# `version` is the SPECIFICATION version (SPEC.md), which is what citing work
# refers to. The plugin implementing it versions independently and is currently
# at 2.7.0; the policy schema is at 1.5. See README.md "Status and roadmap".
version: 2.0.2
